A||||9||pHoOl||GT steering wheel taking a poop||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||10-18-2000||11:45 PM||||Anybody know if there is a way to fix this problem without replacing the whole steering wheel?  I'm hoping for something like " take it off and put it in the freezer for a week"<P>lol, maybe i'll have to try that.  but seriously, it's not getting too bad yet, but i dont' like getting steering wheel goop on my hands when i'm driving around impressing girls.<P>What do new ones (slightly used but still hard) run for?  I thought i saw the same kind of leather wrapped wheel in a camaro, and was thinking of cruising boneyards and trasplaning the center cap.  Looked like it would be a perfect match.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ed||10-19-2000||12:06 AM||||I just put a drop of glue on the stitching where mine was leaking.  That fix has lasted two summers so far.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||10-19-2000||12:16 AM||||Maybe a Diaper hehe <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Or just break out the money and get it refurbished <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||pHoOl||10-19-2000||01:38 AM||||What kind of glue?  I figured hot glue probalby wouldnt' stick well enough.  Wood glue?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ed||10-19-2000||11:57 AM||||Regular 'ol household cement.  The kind with all the solvents in it.  I usually use "Duco" brand.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||10-19-2000||12:21 PM||||Mr Mike's does a recover job for leather.<P>Fiero Store does a recover job.<P>I got a new tan leather wheel from MrFiero a few years ago..still in the box, now on my 88 GT.  Must have been the last one. Don't a$k.  Those leather wheels are rather rare as a replacement part.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||10-19-2000||01:30 PM||||pHoOl, is this a stock GT wheel?  My SE leather wheel took a poop years before I bought my Fiero.  I replaced mine with a Grant GT.  There are a couple $50 ones that look good, and you'll need the correct adapter kit which runs about $10.  Mine is a smaller diameter and is spaced about 2 inches closer to me which helps me for knee and leg room to the wheel.  I like it so much I'd never go back to the stock wheel.  Well, just posting an idea, I seen a couple stock leather wheels on Ebay not too long ago.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||10-19-2000||03:14 PM||||I have a Grant wheel too, it was I believe $50 to $80 (somewhere like that) and had the $10 adapter.  I like it better then the Formula wheel||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||10-19-2000||05:41 PM||||the thick rimmed "sport" wheel, the one with parrallel spokes and the paddle horn buttons is used in a number of GM cars. I've seen them in cavalier and others. Both the leather and the soft rubber versions should be out there. All you need to do to them is change the rectangular cover in the middle.<P>I have a leather wheel and the matching automatic shifter knob. I got the wheel out of another Fiero but the shift knob is out of a transam. I grabbed them up because I am thinking of putting in leather seats. I don't really like leather but with the cost of fabric covers it's not much dif price wise. Once I get the AC fixed the leather shouldn't be to sweaty.||||reg||1
Z||000009||pollock||10-20-2000||09:55 AM||||Love the rubber-grip Grant wheels.  <P>For my GT Pooper Wheel, i cut off the old leather (kept it to make a pattern when i do a permanent repair) and put on a tight-fitting stitch-on leather cover that i got at Autozone for about $15.  It doesn't cover the plastic on the spokes, but it looks alright and is CLEAN.  <P>I think that poop is actually a mixture of glue and a rotted layer of thin foam, based on what was left inside my old leather.||||reg||1
